Z||000004||KRMFiero||10-27-2001||09:41 PM||||Kick Hill in CT has a Red GT on a Jeep frame<BR>there is a Purple SE in umm NH i think on a Blazer frame<P>basically just look for a blazer or jeep (something with same wheelbase) and cut a big whole in the front trunck and lift up your fiero and bolt it down... Figure out how to hook up steering, brakes will be simple, hook up ignition and everything, i would thing it would work, if i were you i would keep the fiero gas tank in to so you can have duel gas tanks, or take out the jeep/blazer one for extra ground clarence<P>has anyone on the forum done this? I am interested in doing it but i want to know if there is anything else involved so i dont get stuck with a pile of crap<P>Kyle||||reg||1
Z||000005||roadwarrior||10-31-2001||12:14 PM||||just get the drivetrain from a subaru and modifie your chasis, or any traversly mounted 4 wheel drive.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000006||MinnGreenGT||10-31-2001||01:17 PM||||I've seen one, but only in passing- I've thought of doing it too, but I just don't have the time or cash to try it.  I found this pic & article (I think on the forum) of someone's 4xFiero.  It is built on a shortened Chevy Blazer Chassis (-2feet).<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fiero4x4th.jpg"> <P>The article itself is too large to post, you can download it here: <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fiero4x4.jpg" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fiero4x4.jpg</A> ||||reg||1
